The Opportunity

The Product & Tech Contract Management Legal team at Netflix is a team of contract and project managers who provide efficient, effective, and risk-calibrated deal guidance and contract negotiation support to the corporate, studio, games, and product organizations. We’re looking for an experienced Contracts Manager to join the team based in our Los Gatos office. 

The Role

As a Contracts Manager, you will work with diverse legal and cross-functional teams and play a critical role supporting Netflix’s Corporate and Product & Tech Teams in managing vendor deals across the globe. With a curious mindset, you'll continuously seek innovative solutions to enhance our processes and drive efficiency. Your ability to work proactively and independently under tight timeframes will be essential as you manage contracts in a dynamic environment. Success in this role requires adaptability and drive to excel in a fast-paced environment, while maintaining the highest standards of professionalism and integrity. If you're ready to contribute to our success and grow with our team, we encourage you to apply. 

Responsibilities

Collaborate with a team of attorneys and contract managers to assist Netflix’s Corporate and Product & Tech teams in managing vendor agreements worldwide;

Draft contracts and lead negotiations on vendor agreements, including payment processing agreements, master services agreements, data processing agreements and security requirements;

Collaborate with internal business clients and cross functional stakeholders;

Optimize and support contract and workflow systems; create and maintain information on our internal legal portal; and

Support all areas of the Product & Tech Legal Team as the need arises, including on new subjects outside area of expertise and special projects. 

Requirements

8-10+ years of relevant experience as a transactional paralegal, contracts negotiator, or contracts manager, working in-house at a company or law firm;

Substantial experience in contract review, structuring, and drafting, as well as negotiating complex commercial and technology agreements;

Experience with (a) financial services and payment technologies; or (b) entertainment media and streaming services are a plus;

Strong proficiency with vendor agreements, particularly payment processors and payments ecosystem, SaaS agreements and software licenses, including related knowledge with data privacy and security;

Experience with contract database systems and/or workflow systems;

Strong analytical capabilities and judgment; strategic thinker with strong problem solving skills and the ability to efficiently manage conflicting priorities; 

Excellent critical thinking skills, and experience applying learnings, and using judgment on vendor deals, drafting templates, providing guidance, etc.

Ability to be nimble and flexible on areas of responsibilities with respect to business groups, types of contracts, operational tasks, etc.

Responsive, comfortable requesting and accepting feedback, and strong communication skills 

Default approach that favors sharing information openly and proactively; and

Strong organizational and project management skills, ability to drive progress on multiple projects simultaneously.


